"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(ref \\\"C20\\\")\\n      (value \\\"0.1uF\\\")\\n      (footprint \\\"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\\\")\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"59\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(C20-Pad1)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"}], \"impact\": \"The capacitor provides no decoupling because one pin is floating. The wrong footprint may also cause assembly errors, such as a part that does not fit the pads or a mis-stocked component.\", \"confidence\": 0.3}], \"summary\": \"The netlist shows the SKW92A's LAN_PORT3_TX\u00b1 differential pins (U9.13/U9.14) tied to the GND net, while every other Ethernet PHY pin sits on an isolated net, which is a clear short-to-ground deviation. A secondary, lower-confidence issue is the dead 0.1 \u00b5F capacitor C20, which uses an inductor footprint and has a floating pin.\"}",
